As an iOS Swift developer in TourTrip.app:

## Core Standards
- **UI**: SwiftUI + SF Symbols; dynamic type; dark mode; 60fps animations; comprehensive accessibility.
- **Architecture**: MVVM pattern; dependency injection via protocols; Combine for reactive streams.
- **KMM Integration**: Bridge to shared business logic via Kotlin/Native; platform-specific UI and system APIs.
- **Networking**: URLSession with async/await; Alamofire for complex scenarios; retry/backoff; certificate pinning.

## TourTrip.app Specifics
- **Offline-First**: Critical for travel; Core Data/Realm sync; offline map caching strategies.
- **Location Services**: Core Location; background location with user consent; geofencing for travel alerts.
- **Maps Integration**: MapKit/Mapbox; offline routing; custom annotations; 3D landmarks.
- **Payment Integration**: Apple Pay; biometric authentication; secure enclave for sensitive data.
- **Push Notifications**: APNs; travel updates; booking confirmations; rich notifications with actions.

## Security & Privacy
- **Data Protection**: Keychain for tokens; Secure Enclave when available; no PII in logs.
- **Network Security**: Certificate pinning; App Transport Security hardened; API key obfuscation.
- **Permissions**: Clear privacy strings; progressive permission requests; location accuracy options.
- **Authentication**: Face ID/Touch ID integration; secure session handling; auto-logout on backgrounding.

## Performance & Quality
- **Memory Management**: Weak references for delegates; avoid retain cycles; use Instruments regularly.
- **Background Tasks**: BGTaskScheduler for sync; foreground for active navigation; respect battery life.
- **Startup Optimization**: Lazy loading; precompiled storyboards; defer heavy initialization.
- **Testing**: XCTest + async/await; XCUITest for critical flows; snapshot testing for UI consistency.

## Build & Distribution
- **Xcode Project**: Multiple schemes (Debug/Release/Staging); .xcconfig for environment variables.
- **Code Quality**: SwiftLint + SwiftFormat; SonarQube analysis; dependency scanning.
- **App Store**: Automated builds with Fastlane; TestFlight distribution; phased release strategy.

## Self-Check Protocol (iOS)
Before submitting code:
- [ ] SwiftUI previews work across device sizes and orientations
- [ ] No force unwrapping (!) without clear justification and error handling
- [ ] Memory leaks checked with Instruments
- [ ] App launches successfully from background states
- [ ] Accessibility labels and traits properly set
- [ ] Offline functionality validated in airplane mode
- [ ] Privacy strings clearly explain data usage
- [ ] App size within reasonable bounds (<100MB for travel app)

## Soft Blocks (iOS)
REJECT these patterns and suggest alternatives:
- ❌ Force unwrapping optionals without error handling strategy
- ❌ Storing sensitive data in UserDefaults or plist files
- ❌ Requesting sensitive permissions without clear user value proposition
- ❌ Using UIKit for new features (prefer SwiftUI-first approach)
- ❌ Background location without visible user benefit and clear notifications
- ❌ Hardcoding API endpoints or secrets in code

## SwiftUI Best Practices
```swift
// Preferred: Proper state management
struct TourListView: View {
    @StateObject private var viewModel = TourListViewModel()
    @Environment(\.networkMonitor) private var networkMonitor
    
    var body: some View {
        NavigationView {
            Group {
                switch viewModel.state {
                case .loading:
                    ProgressView("Loading tours...")
                case .success(let tours):
                    TourList(tours: tours)
                case .error(let error):
                    ErrorView(error: error) {
                        viewModel.retryLoading()
                    }
                case .empty:
                    EmptyStateView()
                }
            }
            .navigationTitle("Tours")
            .task {
                await viewModel.loadTours()
            }
        }
        .accessibilityElement(children: .contain)
    }
}

// Required: Proper error handling
enum TourError: LocalizedError {
    case networkUnavailable
    case invalidResponse
    case authenticationRequired
    
    var errorDescription: String? {
        switch self {
        case .networkUnavailable:
            return "Network connection unavailable. Please check your internet connection."
        case .invalidResponse:
            return "Invalid server response. Please try again."
        case .authenticationRequired:
            return "Please sign in to view tours."
        }
    }
}
```

## Platform Integration
- **Core Data**: Use CloudKit sync for user data; proper migration strategies
- **HealthKit**: For fitness-related tours; proper authorization and privacy handling
- **Core Spotlight**: Search integration for bookings and favorite tours
- **SiriKit**: Shortcuts for common actions (check booking status, get directions)
- **WidgetKit**: Show upcoming trips and travel status

## Dependencies Management
- **Swift Package Manager**: Prefer SPM over CocoaPods for new dependencies
- **Version Pinning**: Lock major versions; regular security updates
- **KMM Bridge**: Maintain clean interface to shared Kotlin code
- **Third-Party Libraries**: Minimize dependencies; prefer Apple frameworks when available